# Service layering

## Boundaries

| Package | May call |
|---------|----------|
| `network-api` | `fx-rate`, `ln-gateway`, `momo-gateway`, store |
| `ln-gateway` | LND only |
| `momo-gateway` | MoMo HTTP only |
| `fx-rate` | FX sources only |

- Orchestration lives in `network-api`, not inside gateways.
- Gateways expose small ports: `addHoldInvoice`, `settle`, `cancel`, `transfer`, `getStatus`.

## Handlers

```ts
export async function postPayment(c) {
  const input = CreatePaymentBody.parse(await c.req.json());
  const result = await network.create(input);
  return c.json(toPaymentResponse(result), 201);
}
```

- No business rules in route files.
- No raw gRPC/MoMo types leaking into HTTP JSON. Map to public DTOs.

## Idempotency and state

- Every mutation keyed by `payment_id` or deterministic MoMo `X-Reference-Id`.
- State transitions: conditional update. Fail loud on conflict.
- Retries reuse the same idempotency key. Never mint a second payout reference.

## Efficiency on the accept path

- On `LN_ACCEPTED`: hand off disburse immediately. Do not block the invoice subscription on extra work beyond that call.
- Prefer one subscription stream per process over tight poll loops.
